摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Unofficial DeepSeek Harness plugin: mobile-friendly UI, Web Push notifications, and Linux Tailscale setup guide","id":"gh:1359420592","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"Smart-DSH","slug":"hikarioyama/Smart-DSH","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Unofficial DeepSeek Harness plugin: mobile-friendly UI, Web Push notifications, and Linux Tailscale "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"DeepSeek Harness plugin: mobile-friendly UI, Web Push notifications, and Linux Tailscale setup guide"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Smart-DSH — Mobile UI, notifications, and Esc-to-stop for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"An unofficial **DSH plugin bundle and Linux setup guide**, not a fork of DSH.\nKeep upstream DSH inst"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"alled; add Smart-DSH for:"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"- **Mobile UI:** full-width chat and composer, logo opens the session list, no logo tooltip or tap t"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"int.\n- **Notifications:** questions and top-level turn-end notifications through Web Push.\n- **Esc t"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"o stop:** press Escape to cancel the running turn, switchable from Settings → General.\n- **Remote ac"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"cess guide:** connect a phone using tailnet-only Tailscale Serve HTTPS.\n- **Subagent task delegation"},{"id":"p4s5","text":":** roles with one exclusive verb each (worker / explorer / hacker / reviewer), a sibling hub with d"},{"id":"p4s6","text":"urable logs, and a subagent conversation tab.\n- **OpenCode Go model catalog:** keep the `llm-pi-ai` "},{"id":"p4s7","text":"OpenCode Go route current with every model the subscription actually serves (scripts + guide).\n- **M"},{"id":"p4s8","text":"ulti-tab reliability:** an optional, guarded shared-HMR workaround prevents upstream developer-updat"},{"id":"p4s9","text":"e connections from exhausting Firefox's HTTP/1.1 connection slots."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This is an unofficial community extension; it is not affiliated with DeepSeek.\nCompatibility is test"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ed against DSH `0.1.2-rc.1`; mobile styles use version-specific\nselectors. Turn-end notifications de"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"scribe agent turn termination, not independent\nverification that every requested task succeeded."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"A self-contained DeepSeek Harness (DSH)\nbundle (`dsh-notify-push`) plus setup notes for the paired r"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"emote-access infrastructure\n(Tailscale Serve + phone). When the agent calls `ask_user_question`, you"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"r phone receives\na Web Push notification with the question text — **even when no browser is connecte"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"d**.\nWhen a turn ends, you get a completion notification whose title reflects the end reason\n[该节后续省略"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"**.\nWhen a turn ends, you get a completion notification whose title reflects the end reason\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Requirement | Why |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| DSH `0.1.2-rc.1` | The bundle relies on `webServer.register`, `connection.requestRejection`, and t"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"he `{ prepend: true }` listener option — verify these exist if your DSH differs (`dsh --version`) |\n"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"| Node `>= 22.19` (23 excluded) | DSH's own requirement |\n| `pnpm` | `dsh plugin` is a thin pnpm for"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"warder |\n| Any Chromium-based browser or Firefox with `PushManager` | Verified on Android Chrome (FC"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"M) and desktop Firefox (Mozilla autopush) |\n| A **secure context** for the phone | HTTPS via Tailsca"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"le Serve (below) — plain `http://<ip>:3080` cannot subscribe to push |\n| Android: nothing extra. iOS"},{"id":"p9s7","text":": Add-to-Home-Screen | iOS WebKit only delivers push to installed PWAs (16.4+) |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Component | File | Role |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Host half | `dsh-notify-push/lib/index.js` | prepended `user-questions/request` waterfall listener"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" + `session/event` (`turn/end`) listener (root sessions only) + Web Push fan-out + HTTP routes (`/ap"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"i/push/*` authed via `connection.requestRejection`, `/push/sw.js` static with `Service-Worker-Allowe"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"d: /`) |\n| Client half | `dsh-notify-push/lib/client.js` | `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({...})` wra"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"pper; local `Notification` while the page is alive; `/notify` popupSelect command for permission + p"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"ush subscribe/unsubscribe |\n| Service worker | `dsh-notify-push/sw/sw.js` | `push` → `showNotificati"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"on` (`requireInteraction: true`), `notificationclick` → focus/open window |\n| State | `$DSH_HOME/not"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"ify-push/` (0600, **not in this repo**) | `vapid.json` (generated on first start, must persist acros"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"s restarts) + `subscriptions.json` (auto-pruned on 404/410) |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The state directory follows `DSH_HOME` (default `~/.dsh`), so nothing here is\nhard-wired to a specif"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"e directory follows `DSH_HOME` (default `~/.dsh`), so nothing here is\nhard-wired to a specific user."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"> **Dependency note**: `dsh` profiles use `nodeLinker: hoisted` in their\n> `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, so"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" the `pnpm add` in step 1 lands inside the profile's\n> `node_modules` and resolves from the linked b"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"undle. If step 4 reports that\n> `web-push` can't be resolved, re-run step 1 and then `pnpm install` "},{"id":"p17s4","text":"in the\n> profile dir."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Then restart and enable:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Expected result: `~/.dsh/notify-push/vapid.json` + `subscriptions.json` appear on first\nstart; each "},{"id":"p20s2","text":"enabled device appears as one subscription; asking the agent a question that\ntriggers `ask_user_ques"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"tion` produces a notification on every enabled device."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Fresh tabs show “No sessions yet”"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"On DSH `0.1.2-rc.1`, upstream `client-hmr` opens a permanent developer-update\nconnection for each ta"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"b. Enough tabs can exhaust a browser's HTTP/1.1 slots,\npreventing fresh session-list requests and We"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"bSocket handshakes. This is unrelated\nto the `dsh-notify-push` notification plugin and does not mean"},{"id":"p22s4","text":" sessions were deleted."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Smart-DSH includes a version- and checksum-guarded workaround that shares one HMR\nconnection across "},{"id":"p23s2","text":"tabs. From this checkout:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"It does not restart DSH or alter browser preferences/session data. Unknown versions\nor existing loca"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"l edits are rejected. This is a separate, optional install step;\ncopying only `dsh-notify-push` does"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" not apply it. See the\nworkaround guide for explicit paths,\nrollback, browser requirements, live-upd"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"ate limitations, and rechecking after DSH\nupgrades."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Esc-to-stop (dsh-esc-stop)"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Press **Escape** while the agent is working and the running turn is cancelled — the same\ncancellatio"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"n the composer's **停止生成** button performs. ON by default, with one toggle\nin Settings → **General** "},{"id":"p27s3","text":"→ *Esc で推論を停止*; the value is the host setting\n`esc-stop.enabled` in the user settings document, so i"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"t follows the account across\ndevices and toggling needs no file edit or restart."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Escape is a shared key, so the listener refuses whenever a nearer surface owns it:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| Refusal | Why |"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| `Ctrl`/`Meta`/`Alt`/`Shift` held, or a key repeat | Browser/OS chords, and holding the key must no"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"t fire repeatedly |\n| IME composition | The input method owns the key |\n| `event.defaultPrevented` |"},{"id":"p30s3","text":" A handler that already consumed Escape wins |\n| the target is a native `input`/`textarea`/`select` "},{"id":"p30s4","text":"| The queue-message editor closes itself on Escape |\n| an `[aria-modal=\"true\"]` element is open | Th"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"e Settings panel owns Escape while it is open |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
